    "ft2232h"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "FPGA I/O are 3.3 V at most and not 5 V tolerant. Lattice's absolute maximum for any I/O is 3.6 V.",
    "Rows run top edge first (PMOD1A, the 5V AUX pins, PMOD1B), then PMOD2 on the right edge and its 5V AUX pins, then the RGB LED header and the flash header along the bottom.",
    "Every PMOD signal goes through a 33 ohm series resistor. The board fits no pull-ups on the PMOD lines. The FPGA has a weak internal pull-up you can enable per pin.",
    "The 12 MHz oscillator feeds both the FT2232H and FPGA pin 35 (IOT_46b_G0, global buffer G0). The PCF calls it CLK.",
    "The second FT2232H channel is a USB serial port: FPGA pin 6 is the FPGA's RX and pin 9 is its TX. The PCF names them RX and TX.",
    "On the main board: user button on pin 10 (active low, 10 kOhm pull-up), red LED on pin 11 and green LED on pin 37, both active low. Pin 37 is also global buffer G1.",
    "Configuration comes from a 16 MB Winbond W25Q128JV flash on the FPGA's SPI pins (14, 15, 16, 17), with pins 12 and 13 added for quad mode. The rest of the flash is free for your own data.",
    "By default iceprog writes the flash. To load the FPGA SRAM directly instead, cut the J15 and J16 traces, bridge them the other way, and use iceprog -S. The design is then lost at power-off.",
    "The CRESET header (J28) holds the FPGA in reset when shorted. The CDONE LED lights once a design has loaded.",
    "Jumpers J3 to J13 are open by default. Closing all of them connects FTDI channel B's FIFO mode to the FPGA, and takes over PMOD2, the red and green LEDs and the user button.",
    "J17 sets the I/O voltage of Bank 2, which is all eight PMOD1A signals, to 3.3 V or 1.8 V. It ships at 3.3 V, and the PMOD1A 3V3 pins stay at 3.3 V either way. J19 (Bank 0 and 1 supply) and J14 (core supply) are there for measuring current.",
    "The snap-off section carries the five LEDs and three buttons on PMOD2. Once it is snapped off, connect it back through PMOD2 with a 12-pin cable.",
    "Needs checking: the PCF and the vendor pinout legend put red on pin 39 (RGB0) and blue on pin 41 (RGB2), and the header silkscreen agrees. The v1.0e schematic's symbol for the optional on-board RGB LED (D11, marked unpopulated) wires RGB0 to blue and RGB2 to red. This page follows the PCF and the legend."
  ],
